| `secrets.scanner.leak_exit_code` | integer | `77` | 3 to 125: not 0 (clean), 1 (the scanner's own error) or 2 (usage), and below the shell's and a signal's statuses | `scripts/scan_secrets.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `secrets.scanner.leak_exit_code` row | Sets the status the scanner is told to exit with on a finding, so a crash cannot read as a finding nor a finding as a crash; a status and a report that disagree are exit 11 (`BACKEND_ABSENT`), because the scanner gave no verdict. A value outside the range is exit 14. Absent, the scan writes `[using default] secrets.scanner.leak_exit_code = 77` to stderr. | the adapter's own exit code, which is 1 for findings | always |
